\left(\frac{\mathtt{j}_k}{\mathtt{j}_{i}}\right)^{3-\alpha}\le R_{S_0^+}^{3-\alpha}, & \text{ if $i < k$}.
\end{cases}
\end{align}
Since $2^{\alpha+1}-4\ne 0$ for $\alpha>1$, we have that $I + \frac{2}{2^{\alpha+1}-4} L$ is invertible, if $R_{S_0^+}$ is sufficiently small depending on $\nu$. Therefore from \eqref{rkksdsdsdsaldksgotj}, we see that  $\mathbb{A}_{S_0^+}$ is invertible. 


